```rust
fn col_alias_overrides(&self, alias: &str) -> Result<Option<String>> {
    // Check if alias contains any special characters not supported by BigQuery col names
    // https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/schemas#flexible-column-names
    let special_chars: [char; 20] = [
        '!', '"', '$', '(', ')', '*', ',', '.', '/', ';', '?', '@', '[', '\\', ']',
        '^', '`', '{', '}', '~',
    ];

    if alias.chars().any(|c| special_chars.contains(&c)) {
        let mut encoded_name = String::new();
        for c in alias.chars() {
            if special_chars.contains(&c) {
                encoded_name.push_str(&format!("_{}", c as u32));
            } else {
                encoded_name.push(c);
            }
        }
        Ok(Some(encoded_name))
    } else {
        Ok(Some(alias.to_string()))
    }
}
```

## Encoding Behavior Summary

The helper logic checks each character against a 20-element array of special characters. When any special character is present, it builds an encoded name where each disallowed character is replaced with an underscore followed by its Unicode code point (`c as u32`), while allowed characters pass through unchanged. If no special characters exist, the alias is returned as-is.

